Drives its own private GC state (its own `gcBindMemory`/`gcInit`-bound arena)
through a scripted allocation/mutation/collection sequence and asserts on
recorded, implementation-independent quantities (numObjects/liveBytes/
collections/totalSwept) shared with `tests/gcdiff.zig`'s Zig-side oracle —
correct regardless of whether the ambient runtime collector ever runs. Every
allocation goes through the private `g` handle, so the ambient collector has
nothing live to find and legitimately never fires under `BIT_GC=stress`.
